from cp4.replay
+0 reload
# CP5 (docs/research/story-cp5-19.md §5): from CP4's end in the Oreburgh gym,
# the Jubilife tag battle (Dawn or Lucas by gender, the team by the starter, against grunts 414 and 415:
# type 75), Route 204 and the Ravaged Path (Rock Smash), Floaroma, the little girl on Route 205 South, the
# Windworks door grunt (843), Floaroma Meadow's grunts (296, 297) and the Works Key, the Windworks: Mars
# (295), and Looker outside, to the moment he leaves.
# The first story chunk starts here: the line after `from` is a save → load, so the chain anchor (a save of CP4's
# end, tests/integration/checkpoints-anchors.ts) and the chain from scratch play the same ticks. The battle
# log and the replay modes are not in a save: this replay asserts its own battles and sets its modes.
# Real battles only: trainers with `battle auto` after the `advance text` that brings them, wild battles
# fought by the waits (`wild auto`); no `party` lines. Trainers whose sight depends on a random look
# (Aroma Lady Taylor, the Windworks grunt at (3, 8)) are talked to from where they never look; Bug Catcher
# Brandon is passed right after he turns (`until state objects[movementType=20].x 182`).
#
# Team and route plan (CP5–8):
# - The starter carries the team and every HM the chunk needs. Piplup evolves (`evolve auto` from here) at
#   its first level up, as Prinplup learns HM06 Rock Smash (Piplup cannot) over Pound for the Ravaged Path
#   (CP5); Cut (HM01, Eterna, CP6) goes over Bubble; Prinplup also takes Surf, Strength, Defog and
#   Waterfall later, Empoleon (36) Rock Climb (CP13). Fly (HM02, CP8) is not needed on the path.
# - Level targets per leader, levelled with `grind` where the story path falls short, healed in between:
#   Mars (Purugly 17) at 20+ (reached on the path); Jupiter (Skuntank 23) and Gardenia (Roserade 22, Peck
#   and Rock Smash) at 26; Fantina (Mismagius 26) at 30; Maylene (Lucario 32, Bubble Beam) at 34; the
#   Veilstone tag grunts (Stunky and Croagunk 26) with the counterpart.
# - Catches: the team grows by the story's gifts (the Togepi Egg, CP7; Eevee from Bebe in Hearthome, CP7).
#   A chosen wild species cannot be caught on every seed (encounters differ per seed and the grammar has no
#   wait on a species), so wild catches stay out of the chain until the replays can wait for a species.
